{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK7a6mGMRH27y2BtKzGS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The autoreloader now watches `manage.py` again. The `utils_tests.test_autoreload` suite passes (21 tests skipped), but I didn't run a real `runserver` and edit `manage.py` to confirm the reload by hand.\n\n**Cause:** When you run `python manage.py runserver`, Python loads `manage.py` as the `__main__` module and leaves its `__spec__` as `None`. In `iter_modules_and_files()` (`django/utils/autoreload.py`), any module without a `__spec__` was skipped, so `manage.py` was never added to the list of files to watch.\n\n**Fix:** In that same function, the `__main__` module is now handled separately. If it has a `__file__`, that path goes on the watch list, and it then gets the same resolving and existence check as every other module's file. Other modules are handled the same way as before."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":859,"cache_read_input_tokens":19158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":859},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd1a2d0c-313f-4ca2-835a-c6099e61b901","uuid":"5450c435-15e0-4b34-a289-5f20ab8ed88d","timestamp":"2026-11-23T03:01:17.504Z","request_id":"req_011ChK7a6XPTeDmadNyx9nbL"}
